# 1. The biggest change: delete the fake integrations

Right now `harbor_adapter.py` is not actually integrating Harbor. It implements its own `HarborTask` and pseudo-RewardKit verifier generator, then shells out to `harbor run`. It also contains a literal bug where a float `reward` gets `.update(...)` called on it.

Replace essentially all of that with:

```text
Moltwork
  generates actual Harbor files
        ↓
harbor CLI / Python API
        ↓
Harbor owns execution
        ↓
read actual:
  lock.json
  result.json
  artifacts/
  trajectory
```

Similarly, archive `flywheel/evaluator.py`.

Its current definitions of novelty and feasibility are things like “does the output contain `novel`, `unique`, `API`, `Docker`, version numbers?”

Those heuristics are actively dangerous once the Lab starts learning from them because the worker will learn to optimize textual artifacts of the grader.

Use real Reward Kit:

```text
deterministic criterion
LLM judge
agent judge
filesystem checks
command execution
HTTP checks
trajectory checks
```

Reward Kit already has 20+ built-in checks and supports custom criteria plus reusable LLM/agent judges. ([Harbor][1])

