# 3. Keep the Letta runtime — this part is close to the right boundary

`services/runtime-letta` is fundamentally shaped correctly:

* explicit worker ID → Letta agent ID mapping;
* persistent agent identity;
* MemFS enabled;
* fresh session per run;
* model/tool configuration;
* trajectory access;
* memory access.

That is the piece I would work hardest on first.

The production invariant should be:

```text
Worker = persistent Letta identity

Campaign WorkerRun
    =
fresh session
+
frozen WorkerVersion
```

And this is crucial:

> **Do not mutate persistent worker cognition during the active Campaign.**

Currently the runtime exposes:

```text
POST /workers/:id/learning
```

which can directly update memory/Skills.

Keep the endpoint, but only use it in:

```text
POST-RUN
```

after a candidate change has been approved.

During live work:

```text
artifact changes freely

worker state frozen
assessor frozen
world frozen
```

Afterward:

```text
candidate memory
candidate skill
candidate process
```

can evolve.

This preserves causality.

