# 5. Harbor should own the complete physical run

This is where I would heavily simplify WorkerKit.

A Harbor trial already gives you an exact trial directory and can preserve:

```text
agent execution
artifacts
verifier artifacts
result
lock
trajectory
cost/model metadata
```

Its regrade mechanism specifically holds the recorded agent execution fixed and runs a new verifier over the recorded artifacts. Source trials are never modified. ([Harbor][2])

So define:

```text
WorkerRun
=
Harbor Trial
+
Letta WorkerVersion
+
Campaign ID
+
WorkerKit Receipt
```

WorkerKit does **not** need to duplicate everything Harbor records.

WorkerKit should witness the important binding:

```json
{
  "campaign": "C001",
  "worker_version": "researcher/v1",
  "letta_agent_id": "...",
  "letta_conversation_id": "...",

  "harbor_lock_digest": "sha256:...",
  "harbor_result_digest": "sha256:...",
  "artifact_manifest_digest": "sha256:...",

  "campaign_git_commit": "...",
  "worker_memory_commit": "...",
  "world_commit": "...",

  "cost_usd": "...",
  "event_chain_head": "..."
}
```

That's enough.

