# 13. Your first live Campaign

I would do this before any generalized experiment suite.

Suppose Oracle produces:

```text
Opportunity O1
```

### A. Freeze opportunity

Create:

```text
campaigns/C001/opportunity/
```

Store:

```text
original Oracle payload
official URLs
rules
sponsor criteria
API docs snapshots/references
deadline
reward
ontology classification
```

Commit:

```text
campaign/C001/opportunity
```

---

### B. Research “what would win?”

Use a **separate Letta research session**.

It reads:

```text
opportunity
official docs
similar public submissions
Hydra prior evidence
```

Produces:

```text
strategy/success-model.yaml
```

Don't auto-assign equal weights like the current `generate_success_model()` does when judging criteria exist. The current implementation simply divides `1.0 / len(criteria)` or falls back to hard-coded dimensions.

For production, record uncertainty:

```yaml
dimensions:
  technical:
    expected_weight: .25
    confidence: .8

  novelty:
    expected_weight: .20
    confidence: .4
```

That is much more honest.

---

### C. Build Assessor v0

Compile the research into actual Reward Kit files.

Use deterministic checks wherever possible.

Use model/agent judges only for subjective dimensions.

Store as:

```text
worlds/C001-assessor/
```

Commit it.

Freeze:

```text
AssessorVersion A0
```

---

### D. Search the solution space

For the first campaign, do this simply.

Have the Letta worker generate:

```text
10 ideas
```

as independent candidate artifacts.

Harbor grades all 10.

Keep:

```text
top 3
```

Ask Letta to research those 3.

Harbor grades again.

Pick:

```text
top 1
```

No GEPA yet.

You need a baseline for whether GEPA later improves anything.

